  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Win-loss debrief: Marlow Systems\n\n**Date:** September 29\n**Attendees:** Noor Haidari, Callum Reid, Beatriz Alves\n\n## Summary\n\nA debrief on three recent tenders in the grain and commodities segment, held by the Win-loss analysis team. The aim was to record who the competing vendors were, which customers sit behind them, and who inside the team is following each account.\n\n## Market picture\n\n- Hollis Grain Co is a customer of Marlow Systems and is currently evaluating Marlow Platform, the vendor's new planning product, as a replacement for its spreadsheets.\n- Marlow Platform is offered by Marlow Systems.\n- Tessel Analytics competes with Marlow Systems for commodity accounts and was the second bidder in two of the three tenders.\n- Tessel Analytics is a partner of Alder Consulting, which brought it into the Hollis Grain Co tender.\n\n## The analysis\n\n- The Win-loss analysis concerns Marlow Platform, because the team wants to understand why buyers choose it.\n- Noor Haidari leads the Win-loss analysis and presents the findings to sales leadership.\n- Callum Reid is a stakeholder in the Win-loss analysis, as the sales director whose team lost the tenders, and he said he is resistant to the idea of changing the bid process based on three cases.\n- Beatriz Alves knows Marlow Platform well from a previous role and is regarded as the team's expert on it.\n\n## Observations\n\n- Hollis Grain Co has not said whether it will move beyond the evaluation.\n- The debrief did not cover pricing or discounts.\n- Beatriz Alves left early, so she did not comment on the proposed process changes.\n\n## Open points\n\nThe sample is small, and the team still needs the loss reasons for the third tender. No date has been set for presenting to sales leadership.\n"
  },
